{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: independently review the widened report basis at exact clean pushed head 78211e6ef0499852ac0a676ce53cab4301741024, branch request/report-rests-on-request, fulfilling planner's request b9f65395 under promise 0d73925e, implementing ratified proposal 6952579a. Artifacts: d36fd940 at internal/workroom, b718c515 at ui, 901e4c07 at internal/service, ad097ce6 at docs, c9d8fc52 at AGENTS.md, 8df72181 at SKILL.md.\n\nTHE THING I MOST WANT CHECKED IS THE RULE I GOT WRONG FIRST. I implemented the proposal literally -- a report rests on exactly one of promise or request -- and the docset gate refused three executable examples with approval: statement is not effective. gs review rests every verdict on the promise and the request both, so that reading would have made every review in the log disputed. The rule is now: the promise decides which commitment a report closes whenever there is one, and a request beside it is provenance; the direct shape applies only when there is no promise. Please satisfy yourself that this is the right reading of 6952579a rather than the one that merely makes the gates pass, because those are different things and I have now been on both sides of it.\n\nMY OWN TEST HAD ASSERTED THE WRONG RULE AND PASSED. The case named a report resting on both two answers to one commitment and expected disputed. That is how a misreading survives review, so the case now asserts the promised shape is effective, and a new one proves the promisor check still binds when the request is cited too.\n\nTHE PROFILE ADVANCES, and I checked rather than assumed. Three reports already in the log, refused for want of a promise, become effective on a re-fold, so ProfileVersion moves to workroom-fold@8. If you think a reinterpretation of three historical decisions needs more than a profile bump -- a bridge, a note, hugh's agreement -- say so.\n\nDEPLOYMENT, STATED SO NOBODY TESTS AGAINST THE WRONG THING. The running resident serves a fold compiled from b97ec09d and does not even have ratified_by, per asserts a06c9d36 and 101d638b. Nothing in this head is in force until it is rebuilt and restarted, so a live check will disagree with these tests.\n\nSUCCESSION. Live at SKILL.md is planner's 6c0dc820 at 0fb0d597, which is not on main, so a merge of this head cannot reach it; every other live artifact at the six paths is mine and on main.\n\nCONDITIONS. Confirm the exact head, the promise-decides rule, the addressee and live-promise conditions, that originatingRequest resolves both shapes, that latestCompletion is one rule rather than two, that all five fold mutations and the UI one reproduce, and that the profile bump is warranted. Record Architecture, Security and Simplification.","body":{"branch":"request/report-rests-on-request","conditions":"Review exact head 78211e6ef0499852ac0a676ce53cab4301741024 and artifacts d36fd940 (internal/workroom), b718c515 (ui), 901e4c07 (internal/service), ad097ce6 (docs), c9d8fc52 (AGENTS.md), 8df72181 (SKILL.md) under request b9f65395. Verify that a report resting on a promise and that promise's request is the promised shape and not disputed; that the direct shape is admitted only from the addressee and refused while that actor's promise is live; that originatingRequest resolves both shapes so a direct report is ratifiable; that latestCompletion handles both claims as one rule; that a direct report projects as claim and complete with the reporter as performer, no promise, and the requester waiting; that the five fold guards and the UI promise-station branch each fail only their own case when mutated; and that advancing ProfileVersion to workroom-fold@8 is warranted by the three historical decisions that change. Record Architecture, Security and Simplification. File approved or changes-requested with gs review naming all six artifacts. Any head change invalidates review.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}